hinder|make-progress-difficult|VERB|make progress harder|To make it harder for someone or something to move forward or succeed.|cản trở|Heavy traffic hindered the delivery of the new shelves.|Giao thông đông đúc cản trở việc giao những chiếc kệ mới.|Transitive: hinder progress; hinder someone from doing something. Hinder need not mean stop completely.|-
impression|effect-on-observer|NOUN|effect on an observer|The feeling or opinion that a person or thing creates in someone.|ấn tượng|The carefully restored hall made a strong impression on the visitors.|Hội trường được phục chế cẩn thận tạo ấn tượng mạnh với khách tham quan.|Countable: make an impression on someone; a first impression.|0
impression|belief-from-limited-evidence|NOUN|belief about a situation|An idea about something formed without complete or certain information.|cảm giác; ý nghĩ chưa chắc chắn|I had the impression that the meeting would finish before lunch.|Tôi có cảm giác cuộc họp sẽ kết thúc trước bữa trưa.|Have the impression that; be under the impression that. An impression is not necessarily a confirmed fact.|1
peel|remove-outer-skin|VERB|remove a fruit's or vegetable's skin|To take the outer skin off fruit or vegetables.|gọt vỏ; bóc vỏ|She peeled the carrots and cut them into thin strips.|Cô gọt vỏ cà rốt rồi cắt thành những dải mỏng.|Transitive: peel a carrot. Peeled and peeling; no peel noun is proposed in this boundary.|-
surprising|unexpected|ADJECTIVE|causing surprise|Causing surprise because it is not what someone expected.|đáng ngạc nhiên; bất ngờ|The quiet garden held a surprising variety of colourful birds.|Khu vườn yên tĩnh có nhiều loài chim sặc sỡ đến mức đáng ngạc nhiên.|Surprising describes the cause; surprised describes the person's reaction. It is surprising that...|0
wait|stay-until-something-happens|VERB|stay until something happens|To remain somewhere or delay an action until someone arrives or something happens.|chờ; đợi|We waited for the guide beside the ticket office.|Chúng tôi chờ hướng dẫn viên bên cạnh quầy vé.|Usually intransitive: wait for someone, wait to do something. Wait on has separate meanings.|0
wait|period-of-waiting|NOUN|period spent waiting|A period during which someone has to wait.|thời gian chờ đợi|The wait for the next ferry lasted nearly an hour.|Thời gian chờ chuyến phà tiếp theo kéo dài gần một giờ.|Countable: a long wait; a wait for something. Distinguish the noun from the imperative wait.|1
